# (build 112) The AUDIO page's VOICES: EXTRA puts an effect on voices of its own and the music plays on
# under it (the default, 111's); LIMITED has the effect take the music's
# channel as the chip's six do, the music's note there stopping (111b's
# PS2_Q_EFFECTS=take)
# (docs/audio.md, "Build 112"). It was Q's: route_probe is built without Q
# and the chip plays, so the line under it said Q ONLY. (build 124) The
# chip's too, with a second chip for the effects (docs/second_chip.md): no
# Q ONLY beside it, and the title's theme plays on through every change
# (each replays the chip onto its new way). Two values: left, right and C
# each flip it.
# The route reads its own settings.json, never the player's.
start new
sound render on
wait screen title
wait ticks 420
press esc
expect escape-menu open
press down
press down
press down
press down
press down
press c
press down
press down
press down
press down
press down
expect audio voices EXTRA
press right
expect audio voices LIMITED
wait ticks 10
shot page_voices_limited
expect sound playing
press left
expect audio voices EXTRA
press c
expect audio voices LIMITED
press c
expect audio voices EXTRA
wait ticks 12
expect sound playing
press b
press b
expect escape-menu closed
